            "review_title": "Review at Mi Quang Pho Hoi",
            "review_text": "Steve J\nToronto, Canada117 contributions\n0\nBreakfast\nOct 2018 • Family\nThey recently refurbed the restaurant and moved location. Now they are just opposite lotte mall by the traffic lights. No air conditioning but lots of wall fans. I don't think one should expect wine and dine with these dishes in residential neighbourhoods.\n\nI took my Vietnamese critic along and it was a thumbs up. The place was full and it was 9:30 on a Saturday morning. We shared a mi quang thap cam and a Cao Lao. It does bring back memories of my travels to central Vietnam. Their Hoi An Chicken rice was also popular with diners I noticed. Will definitely try that next time. Bill was 4USD or 80k VND.\nRead more\nWritten October 21, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
